{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>and it will be evil in His eyes</b> — that is, He does not desire that you rejoice when you take vengeance upon Him." "<b>and He will turn away His anger from upon him</b> — when you rejoice in his stumbling and turn back the anger, He will nullify the decree and turn it upon you, just as you did not show him mercy."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:24:29.981627947Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}